1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Rasmus Anchersen Hansen is named after his father's cousin, living in Bastrup.
2 CONT
2 CONT " Rasmus Hansen owned Huge yard , which was completely parceled out in his time, so there was only a small farm back, and this he sold about 1850 to Kristian Kristensen . Together with their two children moved away from the parish
2 CONC  "
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the son of Hermann Hansen Vamdrupgaard. His two sons Herman and Jeppe live him. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Om Rasmus Hansen står der: "Rasmus Hansen ejede Kæmpesgaard, som blev fuldstændig udstykket i hans tid, så der kun var en mindre gård tilbage, og denne afstod han ca 1850 til Kristian Kristensen. Sammen med deres to børn flyttede 
2 CONC de bort fra sognet"
